---Audience is an effective targeting option that lets you intersect different segment attributes, such as detailed demographics and affinities, to create audiences that represent sections of your target segments.
---@class gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__Audience
---@field name? string Required. Name of the audience. It should be unique across all audiences. It must have a minimum length of 1 and maximum length of 255.
---@field description? string Description of this audience.
---@field id? string Output only. ID of the audience.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the audience. Audience names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/audiences/{audience_id}`

---A bidding strategy.
---@class gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__BiddingStrategy
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the bidding strategy. Bidding strategy resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/biddingStrategies/{bidding_strategy_id}`
---@field targetSpend? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetSpend A bid strategy that sets your bids to help get as many clicks as possible within your budget.
---@field targetOutrankShare? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetOutrankShare A bidding strategy that sets bids based on the target fraction of auctions where the advertiser should outrank a specific competitor. This field is deprecated. Creating a new bidding strategy with this field or attaching bidding strategies with this field to a campaign will fail. Mutates to strategies that already have this scheme populated are allowed.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of the bidding strategy.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__BiddingStrategyStatusEnum Output only. The status of the bidding strategy. This field is read-only.
---@field campaignCount? string Output only. The number of campaigns attached to this bidding strategy. This field is read-only.
---@field effectiveCurrencyCode? string Output only. The currency used by the bidding strategy (ISO 4217 three-letter code). For bidding strategies in manager customers, this is the currency set by the advertiser when creating the strategy. For serving customers, this is the customer's currency_code. Bidding strategy metrics are reported in this currency. This field is read-only.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__BiddingStrategyTypeEnum Output only. The type of the bidding strategy. Create a bidding strategy by setting the bidding scheme. This field is read-only.
---@field targetRoas? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetRoas A bidding strategy that helps you maximize revenue while averaging a specific target Return On Ad Spend (ROAS).
---@field currencyCode? string Immutable. The currency used by the bidding strategy (ISO 4217 three-letter code). For bidding strategies in manager customers, this currency can be set on creation and defaults to the manager customer's currency. For serving customers, this field cannot be set; all strategies in a serving customer implicitly use the serving customer's currency. In all cases the effective_currency_code field returns the currency used by the strategy.
---@field enhancedCpc? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__EnhancedCpc A bidding strategy that raises bids for clicks that seem more likely to lead to a conversion and lowers them for clicks where they seem less likely.
---@field maximizeConversions? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__MaximizeConversions An automated bidding strategy to help get the most conversions for your campaigns while spending your budget.
---@field targetImpressionShare? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetImpressionShare A bidding strategy that automatically optimizes towards a chosen percentage of impressions.
---@field name? string The name of the bidding strategy. All bidding strategies within an account must be named distinctly. The length of this string should be between 1 and 255, inclusive, in UTF-8 bytes, (trimmed).
---@field nonRemovedCampaignCount? string Output only. The number of non-removed campaigns attached to this bidding strategy. This field is read-only.
---@field targetCpa? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetCpa A bidding strategy that sets bids to help get as many conversions as possible at the target cost-per-acquisition (CPA) you set.
---@field maximizeConversionValue? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__MaximizeConversionValue An automated bidding strategy to help get the most conversion value for your campaigns while spending your budget.

---@alias gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__BiddingStrategyStatusEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"ENABLED"|"REMOVED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__BiddingStrategyTypeEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"COMMISSION"|"ENHANCED_CPC"|"INVALID"|"MANUAL_CPA"|"MANUAL_CPC"|"MANUAL_CPM"|"MANUAL_CPV"|"MAXIMIZE_CONVERSIONS"|"MAXIMIZE_CONVERSION_VALUE"|"PAGE_ONE_PROMOTED"|"PERCENT_CPC"|"TARGET_CPA"|"TARGET_CPM"|"TARGET_IMPRESSION_SHARE"|"TARGET_OUTRANK_SHARE"|"TARGET_ROAS"|"TARGET_SPEND"

---A campaign.
---@class gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__Campaign
---@field advertisingChannelType? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignAdvertisingChannelTypeEnum Immutable. The primary serving target for ads within the campaign. The targeting options can be refined in `network_settings`. This field is required and should not be empty when creating new campaigns. Can be set only when creating campaigns. After the campaign is created, the field can not be changed.
---@field targetRoas? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetRoas Standard Target ROAS bidding strategy that automatically maximizes revenue while averaging a specific target return on ad spend (ROAS).
---@field lastModifiedTime? string Output only. The datetime when this campaign was last modified. The datetime is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.ssssss" format.
---@field feedTypes? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignFeedTypesItemEnumList Output only. Types of feeds that are attached directly to this campaign.
---@field manualCpc? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__ManualCpc Standard Manual CPC bidding strategy. Manual click-based bidding where user pays per click.
---@field biddingStrategySystemStatus? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignBiddingStrategySystemStatusEnum Output only. The system status of the campaign's bidding strategy.
---@field name? string The name of the campaign. This field is required and should not be empty when creating new campaigns. It must not contain any null (code point 0x0), NL line feed (code point 0xA) or carriage return (code point 0xD) characters.
---@field targetSpend? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetSpend Standard Target Spend bidding strategy that automatically sets your bids to help get as many clicks as possible within your budget.
---@field manualCpa? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__ManualCpa Standard Manual CPA bidding strategy. Manual bidding strategy that allows advertiser to set the bid per advertiser-specified action. Supported only for Local Services campaigns.
---@field targetImpressionShare? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetImpressionShare Target Impression Share bidding strategy. An automated bidding strategy that sets bids to achieve a chosen percentage of impressions.
---@field accessibleBiddingStrategy? string Output only. Resource name of AccessibleBiddingStrategy, a read-only view of the unrestricted attributes of the attached portfolio bidding strategy identified by 'bidding_strategy'. Empty, if the campaign does not use a portfolio strategy. Unrestricted strategy attributes are available to all customers with whom the strategy is shared and are read from the AccessibleBiddingStrategy resource. In contrast, restricted attributes are only available to the owner customer of the strategy and their managers. Restricted attributes can only be read from the BiddingStrategy resource.
---@field targetCpm? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetCpm A bidding strategy that automatically optimizes cost per thousand impressions.
---@field geoTargetTypeSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_GeoTargetTypeSetting The setting for ads geotargeting.
---@field shoppingSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_ShoppingSetting The setting for controlling Shopping campaigns.
---@field advertisingChannelSubType? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignAdvertisingChannelSubTypeEnum Immutable. Optional refinement to `advertising_channel_type`. Must be a valid sub-type of the parent channel type. Can be set only when creating campaigns. After campaign is created, the field can not be changed.
---@field engineId? string Output only. ID of the campaign in the external engine account. This field is for non-Google Ads account only, for example, Yahoo Japan, Microsoft, Baidu etc. For Google Ads entity, use "campaign.id" instead.
---@field selectiveOptimization? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_SelectiveOptimization Selective optimization setting for this campaign, which includes a set of conversion actions to optimize this campaign towards. This feature only applies to app campaigns that use MULTI_CHANNEL as AdvertisingChannelType and APP_CAMPAIGN or APP_CAMPAIGN_FOR_ENGAGEMENT as AdvertisingChannelSubType.
---@field networkSettings? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_NetworkSettings The network settings for the campaign.
---@field maximizeConversions? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__MaximizeConversions Standard Maximize Conversions bidding strategy that automatically maximizes number of conversions while spending your budget.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the campaign. Campaign resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/campaigns/{campaign_id}`
---@field finalUrlSuffix? string Suffix used to append query parameters to landing pages that are served with parallel tracking.
---@field effectiveLabels? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.StringList Output only. The resource names of effective labels attached to this campaign. An effective label is a label inherited or directly assigned to this campaign.
---@field targetCpa? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__TargetCpa Standard Target CPA bidding strategy that automatically sets bids to help get as many conversions as possible at the target cost-per-acquisition (CPA) you set.
---@field servingStatus? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignServingStatusEnum Output only. The ad serving status of the campaign.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.StringList Output only. The resource names of labels attached to this campaign.
---@field endDate? string The last day of the campaign in serving customer's timezone in YYYY-MM-DD format. On create, defaults to 2037-12-30, which means the campaign will run indefinitely. To set an existing campaign to run indefinitely, set this field to 2037-12-30.
---@field trackingUrlTemplate? string The URL template for constructing a tracking URL.
---@field urlExpansionOptOut? boolean Represents opting out of URL expansion to more targeted URLs. If opted out (true), only the final URLs in the asset group or URLs specified in the advertiser's Google Merchant Center or business data feeds are targeted. If opted in (false), the entire domain will be targeted. This field can only be set for Performance Max campaigns, where the default value is false.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this campaign was created. The timestamp is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss" format. create_time will be deprecated in v1. Use creation_time instead.
---@field maximizeConversionValue? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__MaximizeConversionValue Standard Maximize Conversion Value bidding strategy that automatically sets bids to maximize revenue while spending your budget.
---@field startDate? string The date when campaign started in serving customer's timezone in YYYY-MM-DD format.
---@field percentCpc? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__PercentCpc Standard Percent Cpc bidding strategy where bids are a fraction of the advertised price for some good or service.
---@field biddingStrategy? string The resource name of the portfolio bidding strategy used by the campaign.
---@field dynamicSearchAdsSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_DynamicSearchAdsSetting The setting for controlling Dynamic Search Ads (DSA).
---@field frequencyCaps? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__FrequencyCapEntryList A list that limits how often each user will see this campaign's ads.
---@field campaignBudget? string The resource name of the campaign budget of the campaign.
---@field excludedParentAssetFieldTypes? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignExcludedParentAssetFieldTypesItemEnumList The asset field types that should be excluded from this campaign. Asset links with these field types will not be inherited by this campaign from the upper level.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignStatusEnum The status of the campaign. When a new campaign is added, the status defaults to ENABLED.
---@field realTimeBiddingSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__RealTimeBiddingSetting Settings for Real-Time Bidding, a feature only available for campaigns targeting the Ad Exchange network.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of the campaign.
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this campaign was created. The timestamp is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss" format.
---@field trackingSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_TrackingSetting Output only. Campaign-level settings for tracking information.
---@field optimizationGoalSetting? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources_Campaign_OptimizationGoalSetting Optimization goal setting for this campaign, which includes a set of optimization goal types.
---@field adServingOptimizationStatus? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignAdServingOptimizationStatusEnum The ad serving optimization status of the campaign.
---@field manualCpm? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__ManualCpm Standard Manual CPM bidding strategy. Manual impression-based bidding where user pays per thousand impressions.
---@field urlCustomParameters? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Common__CustomParameterList The list of mappings used to substitute custom parameter tags in a `tracking_url_template`, `final_urls`, or `mobile_final_urls`.
---@field biddingStrategyType? gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignBiddingStrategyTypeEnum Output only. The type of bidding strategy. A bidding strategy can be created by setting either the bidding scheme to create a standard bidding strategy or the `bidding_strategy` field to create a portfolio bidding strategy. This field is read-only.

---@alias gcp.unstable.searchads360_v0.GoogleAdsSearchads360V0Resources__CampaignAdServingOptimizationStatusEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"OPTIMIZE"|"CONVERSION_OPTIMIZE"|"ROTATE"|"ROTATE_INDEFINITELY"|"UNAVAILABLE"

